# Tuning registry (2026-08-23, Layer 0) — live-mutated runtime state, NOT
# an audit trail. config/brick_params.yaml is tracked in git but drifts
# from its live-mutated copy on Studio (heavy_sweep.py's rewrites never
# get committed back) — the tracked file just goes stale. Don't repeat
# that for this one: nt_tuning_params (Supabase) is the real audit trail;
# this file is a fast local cache only. See
# worklog/PARAMETER_TUNING_PLAYBOOK.md §2.3/§2.4.
config/tuning_registry.yaml

# 2026-09-08: applying the exact fix above to brick_params.yaml itself —
# this was the file the comment above was warning not to repeat the
# mistake for, and the mistake had already been made here. Confirmed
# stale (last git commit predates this ignore by 7+ weeks, missing
# XAUUSD/XAUEUR/XAUAUD entirely, defaults section sized for a ~$1 asset).
# It's the same live-mutated-runtime-state-not-an-audit-trail shape:
# heavy_sweep.py's weekly rewrite happens on Studio's local disk and was
# never meant to be committed back. The real, queryable audit trail
# already exists — nt_signal_sim captures brick_size/sl_bricks/tp_bricks
# per signal at generation time, so "what geometry was live for symbol X
# at time Y" is answerable from real per-signal data, not from this file.
# Untracking this so nobody (human or agent) mistakes the committed copy
# for ground truth again — see worklog
# 20260907_REACHABILITY_LIVE_RESOLUTION_AND_SIGNAL_QUALITY_REPORT_SCOPE.md.
config/brick_params.yaml

# Signal-stream local lookback cache (2026-09-09,
# regime_platform/sweep_orchestrator/signal_stream_cache.py) — a local
# SQLite rolling cache of per-tick signal features feeding the meta-
# regime model. Supabase's nt_signal_sim remains the durable source of
# truth (resync_from_supabase() self-heals this file from it); this is a
# fast local working set only, not an audit trail. Same
# live-mutated-runtime-state shape as tuning_registry.yaml/
# brick_params.yaml above. See worklog
# 20260909_CALIBRATION_AND_SCORING_METHODOLOGY_REFRAME.md §6.
config/signal_stream_cache.sqlite

# Local knowledge index (2026-09-10, Phase 1 of worklog
# 20260910_AAPL_REGIME_STALENESS_AND_SELF_LEARNING_SCOPE.md §3,
# regime_platform/services/self_learning/knowledge_index.py) — a local
# SQLite semantic index over the codebase + worklogs + nt_roadmap notes.
# Deliberately never a Supabase table (see that worklog section for why);
# rebuilt nightly on Studio, not meaningful to commit. Same
# live-mutated-runtime-state shape as tuning_registry.yaml/
# signal_stream_cache.sqlite above.
config/knowledge_index.sqlite
config/knowledge_index.sqlite-wal
config/knowledge_index.sqlite-shm

